    "https://careers.suss.edu.sg/job/LecturerSenior-LecturerAssociate-Professor-%28Gerontology%29/1365106366/": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer/Associate Professor (Gerontology)",
      "description": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer/Associate Professor (Gerontology) Job Details | Singapore University of Social Sciences Skip to main content SUSS Careers About SUSS Join Talent Community View All Jobs Find Us on LinkedIn Login/View Profile SUSS Careers About SUSS Join Talent Community View All Jobs Find Us on LinkedIn Login/View Profile SUSS Careers About SUSS Join Talent Community View All Jobs Find Us on Linkedin Login/View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Location All School/Department All Job Type All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Apply now Start apply with LinkedIn Apply Now Start Please wait... Lecturer/Senior Lecturer/Associate Professor (Gerontology) Who We Are As Singapore's first institute for lifelong learning, the Singapore University of Social Sciences (SUSS) champions inclusivity to bring education to all and ensure that they are given equal opportunities to develop to their fullest potential in our diverse learning environment. We advocate for the same for our people. We believe everyone should have equal opportunities and develop to their fullest potential in their careers. Embark on an exciting lifelong journey with us in making a positive difference in your career and serving our society. For more information on Singapore University of Social Sciences, please visit www.suss.edu.sg What You Will Be Doing The successful candidate will join the Gerontology cluster in the S R Nathan School of Human Developnent and will be expected to teach and conduct research in Gerontology and closely related fields. Key Responsibilities Design and teach courses under the Gerontology Programmes Support the administrative and internationalization of gerontology programmes Conduct impactful and community based research on ageing-related issues Develop and enhance gerontology programmes, including curriculum design and student mentoring. Engage with community organizations, policymakers, and industry partners to promote aging-related initiativesand Gerontology Programmes Contribute to university service, including committee work and academic events. Job Requirements A PhD or equivalent in Gerontology, Aging Studies, Social Sciences, Public Health, or a related field. Demonstrated expertise in ageing-related research, teaching, or practice. Strong publication record and ability to secure research funding. Experience in curriculum development, programme leadership, or community-based aging projects is anadvantage. Passion for lifelong learning, community engagement, and public education in ageing. What We Offer At SUSS, we advocate the Spirit of Learning and pride ourselves as lifelong learners. You will gain access to various learning platforms and plenty of development opportunities to support your growth in a meaningful career! Besides that, you will also get: Competitive Pay Package Hybrid Work Arrangement (Subject to Job Role) Medical Benefits Flex Benefits Family Care Leaves Volunteer Service Leaves Wellness & Recreation Activities Lifelong Learning Opportunities Career Development Opportunities through Internal Job Postings and Transfers Apply now » Apply now Start apply with LinkedIn Apply Now Start Please wait... Find similar jobs: View All Jobs, Academic Appointments Home SUSS Careers About SUSS Join Talent Community View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © 2020 Singapore University of Social Sciences. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.suss.edu.sg/job/Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer-%28Core-Learning%29/1363654966/": {
      "title": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer (Core Learning)",
      "description": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer (Core Learning) Job Details | Singapore University of Social Sciences Skip to main content SUSS Careers About SUSS Join Talent Community View All Jobs Find Us on LinkedIn Login/View Profile SUSS Careers About SUSS Join Talent Community View All Jobs Find Us on LinkedIn Login/View Profile SUSS Careers About SUSS Join Talent Community View All Jobs Find Us on Linkedin Login/View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Location All School/Department All Job Type All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Apply now Start apply with LinkedIn Apply Now Start Please wait... Lecturer / Senior Lecturer (Core Learning) Who We Are As Singapore's first institute for lifelong learning, the Singapore University of Social Sciences (SUSS) champions inclusivity to bring education to all and ensure that they are given equal opportunities to develop to their fullest potential in our diverse learning environment. We advocate for the same for our people. We believe everyone should have equal opportunities and develop to their fullest potential in their careers. Embark on an exciting lifelong journey with us in making a positive difference in your career and serving our society. For more information on Singapore University of Social Sciences, please visit www.suss.edu.sg About The Job The Singapore University of Social Sciences (SUSS) is the newest Singapore government-funded university. Since its establishment in 2005, the University has leveraged on its strong relationships with industry to offer a unique applied curriculum for working adults that produces graduates who are confident, highly skilled, and job-ready. In 2014, it began to offer full-time degree programmes to fresh school leavers, with a curriculum designed to develop graduates who embody the 3 Hs: Head (professional competence and job readiness), Heart (social awareness and consciousness), and Habit (self-directed and lifelong learning). To support the mission of the University, the SUSS Core provides a transformative experience for all SUSS undergraduates by focusing on educating the whole person – cognitively, socially, and creatively. The SUSS Core equips students with transferable skills to develop them into adaptive and resilient global citizens who are able to meet the challenges of the 21 st century. These courses aim to enable our students to appreciate complex issues in local and global contexts, enhance their understandings of individuals, communities and relationships, and empower them to contribute meaningfully to society through interdisciplinary approaches and experiential learning. What You Will Be Doing We are looking for individuals who believe and embody the 3 Hs, are knowledgeable in their fields and have an inter-disciplinary outlook, and are aligned with the direction and approach of the SUSS Core to join our faculty team. The responsibilities of full-time faculty members include teaching and developing courses, conducting academic and/or applied research, and being involved in activities in the service of SUSS and outside of SUSS that may include outreach to industry and involvement in industry projects. Individuals who are able to teach in the following areas, or are trained in related disciplines should apply: STEM AI Humanities and Data Science Human Factors / Human-Computer Interaction / User Experience Design Psychology Job Requirements A PhD from a reputable university At least five years of relevant teaching and research experience in an academic institution for senior positions High level of integrity Good communication and interpersonal skills The ability to work independently and as part of our team, keep abreast of developments in their fields, think strategically, and be a role model to our students. What We Offer At SUSS, we advocate the Spirit of Learning and pride ourselves as lifelong learners. You will gain access to various learning platforms and plenty of development opportunities to support your growth in a meaningful career! Besides that, you will also get: Competitive Pay Package Hybrid Work Arrangement (Subject to Job Role) Medical Benefits Flex Benefits Family Care Leaves Volunteer Service Leaves Wellness & Recreation Activities Lifelong Learning Opportunities Career Development Opportunities through Internal Job Postings and Transfers Apply now » Apply now Start apply with LinkedIn Apply Now Start Please wait... Find similar jobs: View All Jobs, Academic Appointments Home SUSS Careers About SUSS Join Talent Community View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © 2020 Singapore University of Social Sciences. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.suss.edu.sg/job/LecturerSenior-LecturerAssociate-Professor-%28Social-Sciences%29/1358236466/": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer/Associate Professor (Social Sciences)",
      "description": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer/Associate Professor (Social Sciences) Job Details | Singapore University of Social Sciences Skip to main content SUSS Careers About SUSS Join Talent Community View All Jobs Find Us on LinkedIn Login/View Profile SUSS Careers About SUSS Join Talent Community View All Jobs Find Us on LinkedIn Login/View Profile SUSS Careers About SUSS Join Talent Community View All Jobs Find Us on Linkedin Login/View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Location All School/Department All Job Type All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Apply now Start apply with LinkedIn Apply Now Start Please wait... Lecturer/Senior Lecturer/Associate Professor (Social Sciences) Who We Are As Singapore's first institute for lifelong learning, the Singapore University of Social Sciences (SUSS) champions inclusivity to bring education to all and ensure that they are given equal opportunities to develop to their fullest potential in our diverse learning environment. We advocate for the same for our people. We believe everyone should have equal opportunities and develop to their fullest potential in their careers. Embark on an exciting lifelong journey with us in making a positive difference in your career and serving our society. For more information on Singapore University of Social Sciences, please visit www.suss.edu.sg What You Will Be Doing Singapore University of Social Sciences is one of Singapore's six autonomous universities and its mission is to provide lifelong education that equips learners to serve society. Home to more than 15,000 students, SUSS provides an applied education that targets both fresh school leavers and adult learners, with a focus on the social sciences. It adopts a flexible and practice-focused learning approach and offers more than 70 degree programmes in various disciplines. Applications are invited for an open-rank faculty position in the area of Social Sciences at the Singapore University of Social Sciences. The successful candidate will join the Behavioural Sciences cluster in the School of Humanities and Behavioural Sciences and will be expected to teach and conduct research in Social Sciences and closely related fields. Job Requirements Ph.D. degree holder in a relevant Social Sciences discipline from a reputable university. Ph.D. candidates nearing completion will also be considered. Candidates with teaching and/or working experience in the relevant area will have an added advantage. Candidates with online teaching experience as well as those who have managed online courses or programmes will also have an added advantage during the selection process. What We Offer At SUSS, we advocate the Spirit of Learning and pride ourselves as lifelong learners. You will gain access to various learning platforms and plenty of development opportunities to support your growth in a meaningful career! Besides that, you will also get: Competitive Pay Package Hybrid Work Arrangement (Subject to Job Role) Medical Benefits Flex Benefits Family Care Leaves Volunteer Service Leaves Wellness & Recreation Activities Lifelong Learning Opportunities Career Development Opportunities through Internal Job Postings and Transfers Apply now » Apply now Start apply with LinkedIn Apply Now Start Please wait... Find similar jobs: View All Jobs, Academic Appointments Home SUSS Careers About SUSS Join Talent Community View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © 2020 Singapore University of Social Sciences. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.suss.edu.sg/job/Specialist%2C-Career-Development/1366422666/": {
      "title": "Specialist, Career Development",
      "description": "Specialist, Career Development Job Details | Singapore University of Social Sciences Skip to main content SUSS Careers About SUSS Join Talent Community View All Jobs Find Us on LinkedIn Login/View Profile SUSS Careers About SUSS Join Talent Community View All Jobs Find Us on LinkedIn Login/View Profile SUSS Careers About SUSS Join Talent Community View All Jobs Find Us on Linkedin Login/View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Location All School/Department All Job Type All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Apply now Start apply with LinkedIn Apply Now Start Please wait... Specialist, Career Development Who We Are As Singapore's first institute for lifelong learning, the Singapore University of Social Sciences (SUSS) champions inclusivity to bring education to all and ensure that they are given equal opportunities to develop to their fullest potential in our diverse learning environment. We advocate for the same for our people. We believe everyone should have equal opportunities and develop to their fullest potential in their careers. Embark on an exciting lifelong journey with us in making a positive difference in your career and serving our society. For more information on Singapore University of Social Sciences, please visit www.suss.edu.sg About The Job The Student SUcceSS Centre (SSC) invites dynamic and collaborative individuals to join our Career Development Office in preparing students to become future-ready graduates who are able to make purposeful and responsible career decisions. In this faculty-track appointment, you will provide academic leadership in the design, development and continuous enhancement of Career Development's curricula, programmes and student development initiatives that strengthen students' professional readiness, employability and lifelong career development. You will work closely with academic schools, employers and internal stakeholders to ensure that Career Development's programmes remain relevant to evolving workforce needs and aligned with institutional priorities. Where relevant, you will contribute to scholarship of practice, curriculum innovation and applied initiatives that enhance student learning and graduate employability. What You Will Be Doing Design, develop, and review curricula, learning outcomes, assessment strategies, teaching resources, and programme frameworks that support students' career development, professional readiness, and lifelong learning. Collaborate with academic schools, employers, and internal stakeholders to ensure Career Development programmes remain relevant to evolving workforce and industry needs. Develop evidence-informed frameworks, playbooks, and resources that strengthen Career Development practices, coaching approaches, and student development across the University. Evaluate programme effectiveness through data analysis, stakeholder feedback, and outcome measures, and recommend continuous improvements. Contribute to scholarship of practice, applied research, and thought leadership in career development, graduate employability, professional readiness, and workforce development. Represent Career Development on University committees and cross-functional initiatives relating to student development and graduate employability. Mentor and guide students through programmes and initiatives that strengthen their professional and career development. Undertake administrative and operational responsibilities to support the successful planning and delivery of Career Development initiatives. Lead the planning, design, implementation, governance, and continuous enhancement of Career Development academic programmes, curriculum initiatives, and student development frameworks that strengthen students' professional readiness and employability. Job Requirements We are looking for experienced professionals with a strong background in higher education, curriculum and programme development, together with a passion for preparing students to become future-ready and professionally competent graduates. A good university degree, preferably with postgraduate qualifications and/or professional certifications. At least 8–10 years of relevant experience in higher education, curriculum development, learning design, career development, talent development, or related fields. Professional certification(s) in instructional design, curriculum development, coaching, facilitation, or related disciplines would be an advantage. Demonstrated experience in designing, leading and evaluating curricula, academic programmes or student development initiatives. Strong understanding of graduate employability, workforce trends, and career development within higher education. Proven ability to build and manage relationships with stakeholders across academia, industry and government. Interest in, or experience contributing to, scholarship of practice, and applied research. Excellent interpersonal, communication, and stakeholder engagement skills. Passion for developing students, with the ability to inspire, coach and mentor learners from diverse backgrounds. Strategic thinking, with the ability to translate institutional objectives into impactful programmes and partnerships. Strong planning, organisational and project management skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deliver quality outcomes. Adaptability, collaboration, in a dynamic and evolving environment. Willingness and ability to undertake overseas travel as required to support partnership development, programme delivery, student engagement and institutional representation. What We Offer At SUSS, we advocate the Spirit of Learning and pride ourselves as lifelong learners. You will gain access to various learning platforms and plenty of development opportunities to support your growth in a meaningful career! Besides that, you will also get: Competitive Pay Package Hybrid Work Arrangement (Subject to Job Role) Medical Benefits Flex Benefits Family Care Leaves Volunteer Service Leaves Wellness & Recreation Activities Lifelong Learning Opportunities Career Development Opportunities through Internal Job Postings and Transfers Apply now » Apply now Start apply with LinkedIn Apply Now Start Please wait... Find similar jobs: View All Jobs, Academic Appointments Home SUSS Careers About SUSS Join Talent Community View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © 2020 Singapore University of Social Sciences. All rights reserved."
    },
